.TH XL-ANNOTATE 1 "November 2026" "xl-Annotate 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xl-annotate \- mark up images and screenshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xl-annotate
[\fIIMAGE\fR...] [\-\-version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xl-Annotate
adds arrows, lines, freehand drawing, rectangles, ellipses, highlights, text, numbered steps,
pixelation, a magnifying loupe, and cropping to an image. Rough freehand lines, arrows, circles,
and boxes are tidied into clean shapes. Marks stay editable until the image is saved; Save draws
them into the file, and Save As writes a copy.
.PP
Each IMAGE opens in its own window, all in one running copy. With no IMAGE, an empty window
opens; an image can then be opened, or pasted with Ctrl+V.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and quit.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save, Shift+Ctrl+S save as, Ctrl+C copy, Ctrl+V paste an image,
Ctrl+Z undo, Shift+Ctrl+Z redo, Delete removes the selected mark, Esc lets go of it.
Hold Shift while drawing for 45\(de lines and squares, or while moving to go straight across.
Ctrl+plus, Ctrl+minus, or Ctrl+scroll zoom; Ctrl+0 fits the window; Ctrl+1 shows actual size.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xl-annotate/config.json
The last tool, colors, sizes, font, and folders used.
.SH AUTHOR
Wesley Hayslip.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xl-screenshot (1),
https://github.com/xlcheese/xl-screenshot
